On 04/16/2013 05:54 AM, Angelita Wong wrote:
> Hi,
>
> I have a lot of variables, and I want to indicate that they are all
> correlated (for purposes of modeling non-random error).
>
> Instead of listing out all the possible combinations, is there an easier
> way to do this?
>
> E.g., instead of listing all possible pairs of correlations....
> var1 ~~ var2
> var1 ~~ var3
> var1 ~~ var4
> var1 ~~ var5
> var2 ~~ var3
> var2 ~~ var4

lavaan syntax is just text. So you can generate any pattern of text
using base R commands. For example:

# produce all combinations
vars <- apply(combn(1:5, 2), 2, function(x)
               paste0("var", x[1], " ~~ ", "var", x[2]))

# create a single string
vars2 <- paste(vars2, collapse="\n")

If you have your other syntax in 'myModel', you can paste them together with

myModel2 <- paste(myModel, "\n", vars2, collapse="\n")

Hth,

Yves.

