Hi,

I want to test the model in Data
Analysis Example 1, Chapter 9 of Enders (2010) “Applied Missing Data Analysis.”  It is a simple regression model with an
interaction effect (gender moderates the effect of well-being on job performance).  Enders recommends imputing the values of the
two groups (males and females) separately to preserve the gender specific means
and covariances.  I have done this using
Amelia.  But now I need to merge the two
sets of imputed data sets in a way that can be read by lavaan (runMI).   The
imputations datasets are *named* (imputation 1 through imputation 5, as I have
set m = 5 for now), but I don’t know how to use this information to merge dataset
1 for females with dataset 1 for males, dataset 2 for females with dataset 2
for males, and so on.  It is not the same
as merging files by variables internal to the dataset (there is no
imputation_ID in the data).  I could add
such an ID to each dataset, but this would be incredibly burdensome if I wanted
50 imputed data sets.  As far as I can
see, ameliabind does not merge datasets (there is no “by” command on which to combine
two dataset).  So, does anyone have a
reference for how to merge imputed datasets while maintaining the
infrastructure used by Amelia and readable by lavaan?

Thanks,

Bill Cook

PS:     I know I could conduct the regression
analysis and test the interaction effect using a multiple groups SEM, but that
seems inefficient, and I envision other applications where this would not be a
solution (e.g., imputing the scores of husbands and wives in an APIM dyadic
data analysis).

